\f0\fs24 \cf0 Author: Mich Lin (shuyulin [at] mit [dot] edu)\
Last updated: 3 NOV 2025\
\
This suite of code is written to process SHAQ (Subjective Habitability and Acceptability Questionnaire) and POMS (Profile of Mood States) for HERA (Human Exploration Research Analog) Campaigns 5 and 6. \
\
Habitat environments: Home/Hotel/HERA\
\
Habitat areas: \
# 1 sleep\
# 2 hygiene\
# 3 work\
# 4 kitchen\
\
BHP Outcomes\
Mood, Stress, Sleep, IndivPerf, TeamPerf, Social Interaction\
\
Psych aspects of habitability\
1 - privacy; 2 - social density; 3 - efficiency\
4 - control; 5 - comfort; 6 - convenience\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 data_cleaning.R\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 inputs: data files from BOX, SHAQ C5, 6 data (home/hotel/HERA) and POMS C4, 5, 6 data\
Outputs: user saves manually at commented lines. rawdata.Rdata (imported data with full columns, not cleaned), workdata.Rdata
\f1\b  (
\f0\b0 cleaned, POMS interpolated to SHAQ mission days, SHAQ baselined data available by individual) \
\
This script imports the data from local working directory and saves as rawdata.Rdata. The mission parameters (campaign, mission, mission day, ID, habitat area) and relevant variables are kept (SHAQ - how, why\'92s for each habitat area; POMS - summary of each subconstruct). POMS is interpolated to SHAQ mission days for comparison. Both datasets are baselined using home values, substituted with hotel values when not available. This is saved as workdata.RData; a wide data format for easier linear modeling is also generated as wide.RData\
\
Missing data analysis for SHAQ (disaggregated by habitat environment) and POMS.\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 SHAQ_sig_habitability.R\

\f0\b0 input: wide.RData (generated from data_cleaning)\
Builds linear mixed effects models on each of the How\'92s predicted by the Why\'92s. Residuals and multicollinearity correlations are plotted. Linear coefficients are hard-coded into radar plots. \
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
