\f1\b \cf0 SHAQ_discrimination.R\

\f0\b0 input: wide (generated from data_cleaning)\
Remakes SHAQ datasets to make it easier to filter by both habitat area and BHP outcomes simultaneously and binds it all together after assigning \'91Habitat\'92 labels. Plots violin plots or ridge line plots with mean and SD error bars across each habitat environment while fixing habitat area, bhp outcome, and PAH. Can plot by aggregate total habitat or by habitat area. Runs linear models for habitat-environment discrimination and post-hoc tests on estimated marginal means. P values are Holm-corrected at the end. Outputs latex code for supplementary data generation. \
