\f1\b \cf0 SHAQ_POMS_analysis.R\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 input: workdata.RData (generated from data_cleaning)\
Visualizes data over each habitat (mood specific) with box/whiskers and violin plots. Checks for normality visually (not much we can do about non normal data according to work done on the archived version of the project). Using the baselined version of the data taken from data_cleaning.R, joins SHAQ and POMS values (this is SHAQ_POMS_baselined_byarea) and also creates an aggregated (over SHAQ) for a total habitat comparison between SHAQ and POMS. Runs repeated measures correlations for each habitat area vs. POMS and the total habitat vs. POMS and stores the correlation coefficients and the p-values in separate matrices. Also performs data loss assessment to understand how much data is being lost through aggregation/averaging if na.rm = FALSE. Builds nlme (syntax is commented) based on selected fixed data, random data should be MD nested into ID. \
